            <div xml:id="d242">

                <pb facs="0278" n="188" xml:id="pg188"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1908</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Francis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-06-03T13:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 3, 1918, 1
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>155. Your 206, May 26, 9 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d242-f1"/> The attitude of the
                    American Government is that it is dangerous for Chinese soil to be used as a
                    base for hostile military operations by a faction of the Russian people. It is
                    possible that such activities may unnecessarily involve China in an entanglement
                    that will embarrass other powers at war with Germany and Austria, Minister
                    Reinsch was so informed on May 6. Do not answer note.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
